{title: Take the Name of Jesus with You (Precious Name)}
{artist: Lydia Baxter / William H. Doane}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 110}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Gospel Hymns Nos. 1 to 6 Complete (Chicago, Illinois: Biglow & Main, 1894), # 47)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Take the name of Jesus with you,
[C]Child of sorrow and of [G]woe,__[D]__
[D]It will joy__[G]__ and comfort give you;
[G]Take__[D]__ it then,__[G]__ where’er you go.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Precious name,__[C]__ O__[Em]__ how sweet!__[G]__
[G]Hope of earth and joy of Heav’n.__[D]__
[D]Precious name,__[G]__ O how sweet!__[C]__
[C]Hope of earth__[G]__ and__[D]__ joy of Heav’n.__[G]__
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Take the name of Jesus ever,
[C]As a shield from every [G]snare;__[D]__
[D]If tempta__[G]__tions round you gather,
[G]Breathe__[D]__ that ho__[G]__ly name in prayer.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]O the precious name of Jesus!
[C]How it thrills our souls with [G]joy,__[D]__
[D]When His lov__[G]__ing arms receive us,
[G]And__[D]__ His songs__[G]__ our tongues employ!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]At the name of Jesus bowing,
[C]Falling prostrate at His [G]feet,__[D]__
[D]King of kings__[G]__ in Heav’n we’ll crown Him,
[G]When__[D]__ our jour__[G]__ney is complete.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
